Z||000029||SteveJ||06-11-2001||08:27 AM||||Toll money is the money you pay to drive on the New York State Truway which they said for 30 years that when the bonds were paid they would eliminate. The day came and went and the tolls are still here and now up for another increase.<P>Welcome to New York. Stop, pay toll.||||reg||1
Z||000030||Ken Wittlief||06-11-2001||09:54 AM||||the day didnt just came and went, the big day came when the NY state thruway was suppose to become toll (troll) free, and NY anounced "we like collecting all this money, so even though we PROMISED we would drop the tolls when the throughway was paid for, we have decided we'll just keep taking your money anyway"<P>   Kinda like if your bank keeps making you send in your car payements, even after its all paid for.<P>   BTW if you jumper the AB swicth on test connector while the car is running it locks the timeing to 10° BTDC, and the check engine light tells you if the car is running open loop or closed loop.<P>   Also am I the only one that keeps a torx 15 on a socket, and a bent paperclip in my reformed ash tray? I have a small pocket knife in the other one (seatbelt cutter).<P>  I was thinking a vacuum formed tray would be nice for these - I think there is room under them to make them a little deeper.||||reg||11
